# Per-machine LANline server settings. Copy to scripts/run-server.env
# (git-ignored) and edit. run-server.sh sources it with `set -a`, so every
# assignment here is exported. These are the same LANLINE_* variables the
# server reads on its own — see `lanline-server --help`.

# SoapySDR device filter. Unset = first enumerated device.
# LANLINE_DEVICE=driver=hackrf

# This unit's measured crystal error, parts-per-million. Determine it
# empirically (see docs/architecture.md#hackrf-frequency-calibration); leaving
# it at 0 is fine for VHF but drifts a narrowband UHF (FRS) discriminator.
# LANLINE_FREQ_CORRECTION_PPM=-8.9

# Allow push-to-talk transmit (POST /radio/tx/key). Off unless set to true.
# A general-purpose SDR keying a real transmitter is a deliberate opt-in —
# see docs/architecture.md's PTT section and mind what you point it at.
# LANLINE_ENABLE_TX=true

# Serve HTTPS so the mic (push-to-talk) and the location button work from a
# browser that isn't on localhost. A self-signed cert is generated and cached
# on first run (one-time "not private" click-through per browser); or point
# LANLINE_TLS_CERT / LANLINE_TLS_KEY at an mkcert-issued pair for no warning.
# LANLINE_TLS=true
# LANLINE_TLS_CERT=/path/to/cert.pem
# LANLINE_TLS_KEY=/path/to/key.pem

# Also dump the pre-Opus 48 kHz mono audio to a WAV (diagnostic).
# LANLINE_DUMP_WAV=/tmp/lanline-rx.wav
